  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"In the late sixties, Philip Corner noticed his friend Alison Knowles ate the same lunch every day: “a tuna fish sandwich on wheat toast with butter and lettuce, no mayo, and a glass of buttermilk or a cup of soup," leading the artist to turn her dining habits into a performance. She did this by inviting friends to join her at a local diner, to experience the same lunch as her, and to write about their experiences... This book is Corner's own take on the lunch, using Knowles' original piece as a 'score'."</subfield>
    <subfield code="u">http://artistsbooksandmultiples.blogspot.com/2017/09/philip-corner-identical-lunch.html</subfield>
  </datafield>
